// Title: Potential File Overwrite Via Sysinternals SDelete
// Sigma ID: a4824fca-976f-4964-b334-0621379e84c4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-06-03 | Modified: 2023-02-28
// ATT&CK: impact, T1485
// Description: Detects the use of SDelete to erase a file not the free space
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1485/T1485.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_sdelete.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "sdelete.exe" and (not((ProcessCommandLine contains " -h" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -c" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -z" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /?")))
